                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": " * asynchronous), the framework uses the \"drain early notify\" call for\n * stopping playback of the current clip before switching to the next one.\n * The \"early notify\" instruction means that the HAL invokes the callback\n * slightly before the playback of the clip actually ends. And this is the\n * moment when \u0027onAsyncDrainReady\u0027 records the current stream position. Thus,\n * the adaptation layer returns to the framework a reset position slightly\n * earlier, while HIDL HAL implementations used to reset the frame position\n * exactly when the playback of the clip has ended. This discrepancy has to be\n * solved. The problem is that the adaptation layer does not have a way to know\n * when the clip has finished playing at the HAL side, so this moment may only\n * be induced based on other events.\n"
